  "solution": {
    "text": "We can find the position of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>β</mi></math> on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>-axis by plotting the lines and their intersection point on the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>-axis.<br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><u><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0027028_AnsExp2_1.jpg\" style=\"width: 303px; height: 314px;\" /></u></strong><br /><br /><mo>∵</mo> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>β</mi></math> lie on the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>-axis and inside the triangle formed by the lines.<br /><br /><mo>∵ &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</mo> <math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>5</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>3</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>≤</mo> <mi>β</mi> <mo>≤</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>7</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>",
